The viewer's own switch for every photograph, for the session, is the stereo layer's "Enable 3D"
(Stereo::Enable3DAction), in the same words as every program on the layer, at the top of the 3D menu, in place of a
second entry called "Not 3D" (ORDER 551c). Off, every photograph is shown flat; "Not 3D" for one file stays in the
layer's menu. Alt+Shift+N switches it; choosing Stereo, Left eye only or Right eye only shows the photographs in 3D
again, as choosing Stereo did before.

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.19.2.
